From: Guohan Lu <securely1g@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Contribute Framework dependencies to the consuming Go workspace

Retain the published go_mod integration. The owner source retains its standalone
go.bazel.work; a consuming root owns its Go workspace and replacements.
Old dependency-version hunks are unnecessary because the source now owns those pins.

Source commit: 1ca814b6f0053fb728d40bfa82be69a4d4eca6bf
Scope: downstream registry integration; not an upstream bug fix.

--- a/MODULE.bazel
+++ b/MODULE.bazel
@@ -25,7 +25,8 @@
 )
 
 go_deps = use_extension("@gazelle//:extensions.bzl", "go_deps")
-go_deps.from_file(go_work = "//:go.bazel.work")
+# A consuming root owns its Go workspace. Contribute the Framework module dependencies.
+go_deps.from_file(go_mod = "//:go.mod")
 
 # Root-only patch selection, matching the management-common owner.
 go_patches = use_extension("@gazelle//:extensions.bzl", "go_deps", dev_dependency = True)
